[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534766936","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112786#issuecomment-3534766936","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112786","id":3534766936,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SsENY","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T21:54:06Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T21:54:06Z","body":"Are the UV2s identical? Lightmapping is based on UV2. If they are different then you can't really compare the meshes","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534766936/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534891938","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112786#issuecomment-3534891938","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112786","id":3534891938,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Ssiui","user":{"login":"machinescreen","id":132695269,"node_id":"U_kgDOB-jE5Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132695269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen","html_url":"https://github.com/machinescreen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T22:22:43Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T22:42:47Z","body":"The plane made in Blender had no pre-created UV2 so Godot generated the UV2 on import. Viewing the UV2s does show a difference but shouldn't they be the same as they were both generated by Godot? It does look like this explains why the lightmap is rotated and offset by half a texel for the imported mesh as the generated UV2 is rotated and has an extra border. I'm not sure it explains why the actual data in the lightmaps is different though.\n\n<img width=\"1240\" height=\"692\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/61f58671-33fb-4049-a7a2-f0643dc26b75\" />\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534891938/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3535075978","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112786#issuecomment-3535075978","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112786","id":3535075978,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7StPqK","user":{"login":"machinescreen","id":132695269,"node_id":"U_kgDOB-jE5Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132695269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen","html_url":"https://github.com/machinescreen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T23:48:51Z","updated_at":"2025-11-15T00:03:03Z","body":"I've looked at the lightmap files more and maybe the change in alignment _is_ also responsible for changing the data within the lightmaps. However this exercise has also uncovered something else that I wasn't expecting. It appears that the light is not being measured in the centre of the texel (as I assumed it would be) but on the lower left corner.\n\nSo in the case of the PlaneMesh. it has no measurement point in the exact centre because there is no corner there. Instead the four surrounding corners are what samples the light and because the lower left corner is what determines the texel value the 'centre of brightness' is shifted up and to the right. In the case of the imported mesh, because of the half a texel offset this does have a corner in the centre so it is able to sample the brightest point though, again, there is a shift up and right because the lower left corner determines the value. However because of the offset the pattern is completely different. A slight twist is that due to the rotation of the imported meshes UV2 the sampled corner actually appears to be the upper left one once the lightmap is actually applied to the mesh. I've tried to illustrate this below. Each coloured box represents the same value of texel and the dot in the corner is where I assume the light is being sampled from. This is in 4.5.1:\n\n<img width=\"338\" height=\"660\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1879e590-f710-4010-9029-82a11600e36d\" />\n\nNow I'm wondering whether this corner sampling also at least partly explains https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112768","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3535075978/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536146874","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112786#issuecomment-3536146874","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112786","id":3536146874,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SxVG6","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-15T07:22:49Z","updated_at":"2025-11-15T07:22:49Z","body":"Sounds like you are on to something. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536146874/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3946983772","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112786#issuecomment-3946983772","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112786","id":3946983772,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rQjFc","user":{"login":"machinescreen","id":132695269,"node_id":"U_kgDOB-jE5Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132695269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen","html_url":"https://github.com/machinescreen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/machinescreen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T19:56:26Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T19:56:26Z","body":"The more I consider this, the more I think this is simply an issue of differing UV2 generation between imported and primitive meshes. If the UV2s were identical, and I think they should be, the generated lightmaps would also be identical. I've altered the title accordingly. I reckon the far more important issue is #112768 as that is what is causing fundamental misalignments in the lightmaps.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3946983772/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]